<title>USA: TABLE - Aracruz Celulose six mos net lower.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Aracruz Celulose six mos net lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> ADR			 $0.136		   $0.493</p>
<p> Net			 16,658		   53,237</p>
<p> Revs		     237,225		  256,061</p>
<p>	   (All data above 000s except per ADR)</p>
<p>NOTE: U.S. dollars.</p>
<p>NOTE: Aracruz Celulose SA said the decrease in net income was due to the fall in pulp prices in international markets and lower interest income on cash investments.</p>
<p>Net income for the first six months of 1997 included a profit of $5.9 million for a non-recurring adjustment.</p>
<p>The company reported net income for the second quarter of 1997 of $5.0 million on revenues of $126.7 million. It did not report comparable 1996 second quarter earnings.</p>
</text>
